 "research": {
  "summary": "Venus's surface is ~737 K (464 C) at ~92 bar of almost pure CO2, hot enough to melt lead. A pizza at 300 K gains heat by convection through dense CO2 and by radiation. With alpha ~ 1.6e-7 m^2/s the 1.5 cm slab has a diffusion time L^2/alpha ~ 1400 s, so the top crust approaches ambient within a minute or two while the core lags. Property values for dough and the film coefficient are assumptions, hence heuristic fidelity.",
